<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norman Conquest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1066</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Norman conquest of England</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Norman Conquest was the invasion and occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> by William, Duke of Normandy, in 1066 and the following years. William defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson">Harold Godwinson</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hastings">Battle of Hastings</a> on 14 October 1066 and was crowned on Christmas Day. Risings were suppressed by 1071, and a Norman aristocracy and church hierarchy replaced the English elite.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norman-conquest.jpg" alt="Norman Conquest" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amitchell125 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Norman-conquest-1066.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
